# EMBER's static page needs no environment variables to run. The one secret is
# the NASA FIRMS MAP_KEY, used ONLY by the serverless function api/firms.js.
# It is never sent to the browser and never written into any source file.
#
# Vercel:  Project -> Settings -> Environment Variables -> add
#            FIRMS_MAP_KEY = <your key>   (Production + Preview + Development)
#          then redeploy.
# Local:   copy this file to .env.local, fill in the value, run `npm run dev`
#          and open http://localhost:3000 (a plain file:// open has no /api, so
#          the app falls back to its cached scenario and says so).
#
# Free key + instant signup: https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=

# Open-Meteo needs no key (called straight from the browser). If either live
# call fails (offline, no /api, rate limit, key missing), the app falls back to
# its deterministic cached scenario and says so honestly in the Data Sources
# panel -- it never claims LIVE for data that didn't arrive. USGS 3DEP, ESA
# WorldCover and OpenStreetMap/Overpass stay procedural (see README/CHANGELOG).
